.TH "HTMLIMAGEELEMENT.Y" "3JS" "August 12, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLImageElement.y \- HTMLImageElement: y property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The read\-only \f[B]\f[CB]y\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]HTMLImageElement\f[R] interface indicates the y\-coordinate of the
\f[CR]<img>\f[R] element\(cqs top border edge relative to the root
element\(cqs origin.
.SH VALUE
An integer value indicating the distance in pixels from the top edge of
the element\(cqs nearest root element to the top edge of the
\f[CR]<img>\f[R] element\(cqs border box.
The nearest root element is the outermost \f[CR]<html>\f[R] element that
contains the image.
If the image is in an \f[CR]<iframe>\f[R], its \f[CR]y\f[R] is relative
to that frame.
.PP
In the diagram below, the top border edge is the top edge of the blue
padding area.
So the value returned by \f[CR]y\f[R] would be the distance from that
point to the top edge of the content area.
[IMAGE: Diagram showing the relationships between the various boxes
associated with an element]
